WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
An armchair.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.520
A fire burning low.

3
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.530
A book on the table.

4
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.940
In 1891, a young Yeats imagines
the woman he loves grown old:

5
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.960
"When you are old and grey and full of
sleep," He tells her she'll take down his

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.710
book, and read, and dream.

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.140
His poem ends with Love who "hid
his face amid a crowd of stars."

8
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.270
So is this a tender love
poem, or is it a warning?

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.490
In this mission, you'll see
how he speaks straight to her,

10
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.280
and gives her a future in his own words.

11
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.270
You'll compare the many
who loved her with one man,

12
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.060
and follow Love up into the stars.

13
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.880
Your mission: decide what
kind of poem this really is.
